        "Rows: 1 as printed. No totals.",
        "1936: first '8' is a damaged type (right side open, looks like 'ε'); read as 8.",
        "Check pass CK03: 1936 '18,027,041' re-read at high zoom. The second digit has lost its right-hand strokes, leaving an 'ε'-like left half with a waist at mid-height and the upper loop curling back at top right; its height matches the 8 of '8,575,656' in the same row, not the taller 6s. No other digit has that left contour (6 has no waist; 3 is open on the left; 0 has no waist). Certain: 8. Value kept; not decided from any total (the table prints none)."
      ],
